{
  "company_name": "HydroFlow Energy",
  "industry": "Power Generation",
  "use_case": "Hydroelectric turbine optimization and reservoir management",
  "space_title": "HydroFlow Energy - Hydro Optimization & Reservoir Mgmt 💧",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Power Generation\n\n**Use case:** Hydroelectric Turbine Optimization & Reservoir Management\n\nHydroFlow Energy — hydro fleet analytics across 20 turbines (Francis, Kaplan, Pelton, Bulb) and their dams/reservoirs. Plant Managers and Hydrologists use this space to optimize turbine dispatch against water availability and environmental flow constraints; the CFO and Fleet Performance team use it to quantify spillway losses, drought-risk revenue exposure, and storage-vs-generation tradeoffs.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Turbine efficiency (%) — Francis ~93-95%, Kaplan ~90-94%, Pelton ~90-92%, Bulb ~87-93%\n- Capacity factor (hydro) — fleet target ~40%; varies with hydrology\n- Water flow rate (m³/s) — dispatch headroom indicator\n- Hydraulic head (m) — site-specific power potential driver\n- Reservoir storage (%) — days-of-generation buffer\n- Spill volume (m³) — unrecoverable energy loss\n- Environmental flow compliance — regulatory and ESG metric\n- Drought-risk band — forward generation risk\n\n**Data sources**\n- `turbine_units` — daily generation, efficiency, water flow, operating status per turbine\n- `flow_readings` — inflow, outflow, precipitation, snowmelt, head, env-flow compliance\n- `reservoir_snapshots` — weekly water level, storage %, spill, generation potential, drought risk",
  "schema_basename": "hydro_optimization",
