  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports hydro turbine optimization and reservoir management for a 20-turbine fleet of Francis, Kaplan, Pelton, and Bulb units. Personas: Plant Manager (generation_mwh, efficiency_pct, operating_status), Hydrologist (inflow/outflow, head_meters, snowmelt_contribution_pct), Trading desk (generation_potential_mwh, days_of_storage), and CFO (spill_volume_m3 revenue loss, drought_risk exposure).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Turbine efficiency = efficiency_pct; benchmarks: Francis 93-95%, Kaplan 90-94%, Pelton 90-92%, Bulb 87-93%.\n- Capacity factor (implied) = total_generation_mwh / nameplate; hydro fleet target ~40%.\n- Hydraulic head = head_meters; site-specific; Pelton typical >200m, Bulb/Kaplan low-head <30m.\n- Water flow = water_flow_m3s through turbine; combined with head determines power output.\n- Reservoir storage = storage_pct; <30% indicates drought stress; >90% spillway risk.\n- Days of storage = days_of_generation; forward dispatch buffer; <30 days requires conservation mode.\n- Environmental flow compliance — Non-Compliant = FERC/regulatory violation risk.\n- Drought risk band: Low / Moderate / High / Severe — High+ requires conservation dispatch.\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - generation_kpi_monthly (source: turbine_units) — dims: record_date, turbine_type, dam_name, operating_status; measures: total_generation_mwh, avg_efficiency_pct, avg_water_flow, generating_turbine_count, total_turbine_count, max_generation_mwh.\n  - reservoir_kpi_monthly (source: reservoir_snapshots) — dims: snapshot_date, dam_name, drought_risk; measures: avg_storage_pct, total_spill_volume, avg_generation_potential, avg_days_of_storage, high_drought_risk_count, total_water_level_m, unique_turbine_count, max_water_level_m.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. turbine_id, turbine_name, inflow_m3s, outflow_m3s, head_meters, env_flow_compliance, snowmelt_contribution_pct).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Show monthly total hydro generation MWh by turbine type for the trailing 12 months.",
    "Top 10 turbines by average efficiency percentage over the last 90 days.",
    "Which dams are currently at High or Severe drought risk, and what is their average days of storage?",
    "How has total spill volume trended month-over-month, and which dams contribute most?",
    "Which flow readings show environmental flow non-compliance this year, and at which dams?",
    "Top 10 dams by total water level meters this quarter — and how does that compare to last quarter?",
    "What is the monthly trend in average reservoir storage percentage across the fleet?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "How does peak energy generated in mwh compare across turbine units?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT record_date, MEASURE(max_generation_mwh) AS max_generation_mwh",
        "FROM {fqn}.generation_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY record_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total energy generated in mwh trended over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT record_date, MEASURE(total_generation_mwh) AS total_generation_mwh",
        "FROM {fqn}.generation_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY record_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What has been the peak reservoir water level in meters above datum each month?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, MEASURE(max_water_level_m) AS max_water_level_m",
        "FROM {fqn}.reservoir_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total water level m changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, MEASURE(total_water_level_m) AS total_water_level_m",
        "FROM {fqn}.reservoir_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "Which turbine units have the highest total *?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT turbine_name, SUM(*) AS record_count, SUM(water_flow_m3s) AS total_water_flow_m3s",
        "FROM {fqn}.turbine_units",
        "WHERE operating_status = 'Maintenance'",
        "GROUP BY turbine_name",
        "ORDER BY total_water_flow_m3s DESC",
        "LIMIT 10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total water inflow rate in m3/s over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT reading_date, SUM(inflow_m3s) AS total_inflow_m3s",
        "FROM {fqn}.flow_readings",
        "GROUP BY reading_date ORDER BY reading_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has the average reservoir storage as percentage of capacity changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, AVG(storage_pct) AS avg_storage_pct",
        "FROM {fqn}.reservoir_snapshots",
        "GROUP BY snapshot_date ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    }
  ],
